  "worked_solution": "The constant $D$ represents a vertical shift of the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2}).$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the given curve is a tangent function that's been shifted **up** by $\\frac{4}{3}$ units. So, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})+\\frac{4}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $D=\\frac{4}{3}.$",
